#!/usr/bin/env python3
"""The runner host's supervisor (user `rfrunner`; stdlib only). Layout: /opt/rf-runner/slots.json.

  rf-supervisor run SLOT                 the slot's loop (rf-slot@SLOT.service)
  rf-supervisor test SLOT SCRIPT [--tar FILE] [--timeout S] [--out FILE]
                                         one VM of the slot without GitHub: the guest runs SCRIPT as
                                         `runner` (FILE unpacked in its home) and powers off; prints
                                         the script's output
  rf-supervisor host-fingerprint SLOT    the host's half of the machine fingerprint (JSON)
  rf-supervisor status                   = rf-status

The loop, per slot: a just-in-time runner config from the token broker (rf-jit, which alone
holds the GitHub token; name rf-SLOT-UUID, the slot's labels) -> a qcow2 overlay of the current
golden image -> a seed ISO (label `cidata`: meta-data, user-data, network-config, rf-host.json =
the host's facts, rf-proxy = the proxy URL, rf-jitconfig) -> QEMU/KVM (seccomp sandbox, no memory
merging) paused, every vCPU thread pinned to its host CPU, QEMU's own threads on the host CPUs,
then started -> the guest's rf-job runs `run.sh --jitconfig` (one job) and powers off -> the
runner registration (through the broker), the overlay and the seed are deleted -> again.

The guest writes the runner's output to its third serial port (runner.log here), from which the
supervisor reads the phases ("Listening for Jobs", "Running job: NAME", "Job NAME completed with
result: R"; guest text is reduced to printable ASCII before it is logged or stored). Limits: no
listener within boot_limit_s, or no job within idle_limit_s -> the VM is recycled; a job running
past the slot's hard_limit_s, a serial log over 256 MiB, an overlay over the slot's disk_limit_gb,
or less than free_floor_gb free under /var/lib/rf-runner -> the VM is killed. Drain: while
/var/lib/rf-runner/drain exists no VM is started and a VM without a job is stopped. Bench first:
while the bench VM runs a job (run/bench-busy), the light slots take no new job (a running light
job finishes; an idle light VM is stopped). Broker and GitHub errors, and VMs whose runner never
connects, back off exponentially (30 s .. 30 min, jittered). Every VM's facts (runner, image,
sha256 of rf-host.json, job, start, end, reason) are appended to the slot's run/SLOT/jobs.log
(append-only). State for rf-status: /var/lib/rf-runner/run/SLOT/state.json.
"""
